WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Connection Info opens the PostgreSQL assessment dashboard in New Relic.

2
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:58.000
It already shows the earlier tests: failover, replication and point-in-time recovery all passed.

3
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Back in RunShore, Assessment runs the point-in-time recovery test.

4
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:33.000
It seeds orders 5001 to 5003 and takes a real backup.

5
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:43.000
It writes marker order 9999 and records its commit time as the recovery target.

6
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:50.000
It waits until the log is archived, proving the target can be replayed, then writes order 10000, which must not survive recovery.

7
00:01:50.000 --> 00:03:09.000
A new cluster is cloned from the backup and recovered to the target time. The Kubernetes Monitor shows the clone start.

8
00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:16.000
The assessment finishes in 2 minutes 2 seconds.

9
00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:40.000
The clone has orders 5001 to 5003 and 9999, and not order 10000. Point-in-time recovery passes, and the clone is removed.

